 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 507834,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Solve the formula <span data-math=\"I = Prt\">I = Prt</span> for <span data-math=\"t\">t</span>. This formula is used to calculate simple interest <span data-math=\"I\">I</span>, for a principal <span data-math=\"P\">P</span>, invested at a rate <span data-math=\"r\">r</span>, for <span data-math=\"t\">t</span> years.\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Solve <span data-math=\"I = Prt\"></span> for <i>t</i>. Treat <i>t</i> as the variable and everything else as “constants.”</p>\n<p>You can skip to Step 4: Make the coefficient of the variable term equal to 1.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{I}{{Pr}} = \\frac{{Prt}}{{Pr}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{I}{{Pr}} = t\"></span></p>\n<p>Alternate answer option: <span data-math=\"t = \\frac{I}{{Pr}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 5: Checking is left to you.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"t = \\frac{I}{{\\text{P}}r}\">t = I/{\\text{P}}r</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
